  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through Sunday)\nIssued at 1224 AM CST Mon Nov 9 2026\n\nThe last of the rain chances shift southeastward out of the region \nfrom Tuesday night towards Wednesday morning. Wednesday otherwise \ntrends as the warmest day of the week with some possible heating \nattributed to the approach of a weak front and any downsloping \neffects from terrain with a light westerly to northwesterly surface \nflow. Some locations may touch 80 degrees Wednesday afternoon. The \nweak front moves across the area Wednesday night and provides a \ndrier airmass to filter in. This looks to lead to a cooler and more \nrefreshing Thursday under sunny skies. A secondary front may then \narrive into early Friday, which could help reinforce the dry and \ncooler airmass. Friday and Saturday mornings could start off chilly \nwhere the low-lying valleys in the Hill Country could dip as low \nas the upper 30s.\n\nWhile some key differences remain, the most recent 00Z medium range \ndeterministic guidance has fallen much more into line with each \nother in comparison to the 12Z guidance with regards to the next \npossible pattern change when a fairly progressive upper level low \ncould advance across the region from the west sometime late next \nweekend into the following Monday. This reintroduces area rain \nchances (20-40%) into the forecast across the area.",
